A||N||14||pherder||It drives!!!!!!  RE:  ALL RED FIEROS ... LOOK HERE!||||6||
Z||000000||pherder||09-04-2000||02:17 PM||||FINALLY, it drives!!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27656436&Sequence=0"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27656439&Sequence=0"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27656442&Sequence=0"> <P>Project 88 Coupe w/HO Quad 4 and Isuzu 5 speed w/3.83:1 FDR is almost complete!!!<P>This week I will get it licensed for the street, get the wheels aligned and touch up the places I nicked the monochromic red paint in the years I have been trying to get this car together.  <P>What you see here is almost a totally NEW Fiero.  I have replaced or renewed EVERYTHING on or in the car.<P>Still have to get and install the Mr. Mikes leather seats.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  It is good to see it DRIVEN out of the garage for once!!!<P>Paul<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-04-2000||03:07 PM||||Ok, so I'll give you my address so that you can deliver that beauty to me!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Wow!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||pherder||09-04-2000||03:31 PM||||Forgot one thing that is REQUIRED to be made functional ... the air conditioning!!!!!<P>Today we MIGHT not hit 100 degree F for the first time in over 17 straight days ...<P>Paul (melting in Kansas)||||reg||12
Z||000003||StuGood||09-04-2000||04:28 PM||||Beautiful - excellent work.  Guess you're going for that baked-on finish    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> , eh?<P>I love it - it looks so... innocent. It'll be fun to blow somebody away and comment, offhand-like, "well, I guess it's okay for a four- cylinder job...."      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>By the way, Memphis is too far - don't put yourself out so much.  Just deliver it to me in Wichita, thank you     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ...<B>after</B> you get the A/C going, of course     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">         <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-04-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000004||Black88GT||09-04-2000||04:49 PM||||Paul you should put some aftermarket wheels on that bad boy.  I bet some 17s or even 18s would really complete it.  I mean the gold wheels are ok I guess but since your car isn't stock at all I would get some big rims and scoops etc.  Discount tire direct has the best price I have found for rims, and tirerack.com has best price for tires.  Thats just in the brands I have looked at though it may be different for other types.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
Z||000005||Raydar||09-04-2000||10:13 PM||||Paul, Nice job!<BR>I wouldn't change a thing. You've got a great sleeper, there. Looks like a Formula.<BR>I can only imagine the sound.<P>Get that AC operational. <BR>The AC in my truck died, three weeks ago, on the hottest day of the year.<BR>Sweating all over your upholstery sucks!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||14
Z||000006||pherder||09-04-2000||10:23 PM||||Actually, I planned on cutting off the roof at one time and making it into a convertible.<P>My plan was to show the car as an 1990 Fiero Spyder with the optional HO Quad 4.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I had a copy of an original window sticker in electronic form that I modified to make it look like it was the real thing (for a 1990 vehicle) but couldn't decide how to get by the VIN (being a real 88, I couldn't legally change my VIN to have the correct letter code for 1990).<P>The reason I didn't continue with the project was the convertible kit was never finished that I had paid for.  I did get my $$ back.  <P>So, that is why I have the 15" stock wheels on the car ... I wanted it to look like it came right off the showroom floor.  Now that I am NOT going to make it a convertible ... it may become a PISA Artero.  The body is hanging in my shop's rafters.  Then it would get a set of Diablo look-a-like 17" wheels.<P>Paul||||reg||1
