Z||000008||ChadMan||09-05-2000||08:53 AM||||Aw, Paul, don't turn your Coupe into an Artero!  It's beautiful as it is.  And I think your gold wheels look great with the beechwood interior.  I bet it handles great, too - I hear the Quad 4 weighs about 90 lbs less than the Iron Duke.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric_PA||09-06-2000||12:56 PM||||Great job Paul! I am starting my Quad swap in two weeks. It will be going into a Fastback GT. Check out this web site for performance parts for the Quad 4. <A HREF="http://www.genertecracing.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.genertecracing.com</A>  They offer a lot of performance parts and are glad to help people who have done hybrids. They have a 600HP Sunfire!!! Well anyway, keep it like it is, it looks great. Have you been able to check out it's acceleration yet? I finally got a ride in one at the Kick Hill Farms Fiero meet. It is a well worth swap.<P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||09-06-2000||11:45 PM||||AWESOME!!! Keep the wheels. They look great against the interior. I AutoX'ed a Quad4 Fiero on Monday...It would smoke any stock V6 I've ever driven.||||reg||14
Z||000011||pherder||09-10-2000||02:10 PM||||Black88GT,<P>You asked ... you get to see!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=28075947&Sequence=0"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=28075949&Sequence=0"> <P>Took off the stock gold GT wheels to insure the caliper bolts were locktighted in and to adjust the front end toe and thought ... why not put on the new 16" wheels!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000012||Songman||09-10-2000||08:37 PM||||As much as I loved it with the factory gold wheels... the new wheels make it look even better! That is one beautiful car!||||reg||14
Z||000013||Cheever2||09-10-2000||09:10 PM||||Very nice, indeed.  My stock red 88 coupe ("Hot Wax") was purchased from the original owner in January, knowing the A/C was missing a part somewhere. I thought there would be plenty of time to fix it before summer but here it is, 109 in Houston last week.  Paul, did you swap the engine yourself? ||||reg||14
Z||000014||pherder||09-10-2000||09:22 PM||||Cheever2,<P>Yes.  I used NO kit.  Had everything custom made to fit.<P>Go to  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447</A>  to see pictures of the fun and games I have had getting this far.  <P>BTW, from pulling the original 2.5 L out until the last install of the HO Quad4 assembly, I have 16 removals and installs!! (8 of each!) I timed myself the last time I pulled the engine to correct yet another problem and had the assembly out of the car in 35 minutes!!!  The ONLY thing I did have to do to remove the engine/transaxle assembly was to drain the coolant ... I hadn't put in any yet ... just in case.<P>BTW, the wheels WERE for my 88 GT project BUT since they look SO GOOD on the 88 Coupe, they might just remain there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
